# medicine.kb — how the body fails, what is done about it, and the public-health facts that a
# general education carries.
#
# Every line here is textbook-level and general. Nothing in this file is advice about a person:
# a fact store that says "fever is a raised body temperature" is doing its job, and one that
# reads back a dose to someone is doing something this corpus deliberately does not equip it for.

# --- concepts ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
medicine | is_a=discipline | purpose=preventing and treating disease | involves=diagnosis | involves=treatment | involves=prevention
disease | is_a=condition | means=a disorder of structure or function in the body | has_kind=infectious disease | has_kind=chronic disease | has_kind=genetic disease
symptom | is_a=sign of illness | means=something the patient notices | purpose=pointing towards a diagnosis
diagnosis | is_a=clinical process | purpose=identifying which disease a patient has | requires=history | requires=examination | requires=tests@0.7
pathogen | is_a=microorganism | capable_of=cause disease | has_kind=bacterium | has_kind=virus | has_kind=fungus | has_kind=parasite
infection | is_a=disease process | occurs_when=a pathogen enters and multiplies in the body | causes=fever@0.7 | causes=inflammation
inflammation | is_a=body response | causes=redness | causes=swelling | causes=heat | causes=pain | purpose=isolating and repairing damage
fever | is_a=symptom | means=a body temperature above the normal range | occurs_when=the immune system responds to infection
immunity | is_a=body state | means=protection against a particular pathogen | requires=prior exposure or vaccination
antibody | is_a=protein | purpose=recognising and neutralising a specific pathogen | requires=the immune system
vaccine | is_a=medical preparation | purpose=teaching the immune system to recognise a pathogen | causes=immunity without the disease | inventor=Edward Jenner
antibiotic | is_a=medicine | purpose=killing or stopping bacteria | has_property=useless against a virus | causes=resistance when overused
antibiotic resistance | is_a=public health problem | occurs_when=bacteria survive and multiply despite an antibiotic | causes=treatments that stop working | requires=careful prescribing to slow
epidemic | is_a=disease event | means=a sharp rise in cases of a disease in a region
pandemic | is_a=disease event | means=an epidemic that has spread across countries and continents
quarantine | is_a=public health measure | purpose=separating people who may have been exposed | causes=slower spread
public health | is_a=field | purpose=protecting the health of populations | involves=sanitation | involves=vaccination | involves=surveillance

# --- common conditions -------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
common cold | is_a=infectious disease | requires=a virus | causes=a runny nose | causes=a sore throat | has_property=self limiting
influenza | is_a=infectious disease | requires=a virus | causes=fever | causes=muscle ache | has_property=not treatable with antibiotics
tuberculosis | is_a=infectious disease | requires=a bacterium | located_in=the lungs | causes=a persistent cough
malaria | is_a=infectious disease | requires=a parasite | occurs_when=an infected mosquito bites a person | causes=cycles of fever
diabetes | is_a=chronic disease | means=a condition in which blood sugar is not properly regulated | requires=insulin or other treatment | causes=damage to nerves and vessels over time | has_kind=type one diabetes | has_kind=type two diabetes
hypertension | is_a=chronic disease | also_known_as=high blood pressure | causes=strain on the heart and vessels | has_property=often without symptoms
asthma | is_a=chronic disease | located_in=the airways | causes=wheezing | causes=breathlessness | occurs_when=airways narrow in response to a trigger
anaemia | is_a=blood condition | means=too few red blood cells or too little haemoglobin | causes=tiredness | requires=iron in the commonest form
allergy | is_a=immune reaction | occurs_when=the immune system responds to a harmless substance | causes=itching | causes=swelling
stroke | is_a=medical emergency | occurs_when=blood flow to part of the brain is interrupted | causes=sudden weakness on one side | requires=immediate treatment
heart attack | is_a=medical emergency | occurs_when=blood flow to part of the heart muscle is blocked | causes=chest pain | requires=immediate treatment
cancer | is_a=disease | means=uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells | capable_of=spread to other tissues | has_kind=lung cancer | has_kind=breast cancer
fracture | is_a=injury | means=a break in a bone | requires=immobilisation to heal
dehydration | is_a=condition | occurs_when=the body loses more fluid than it takes in | causes=thirst | causes=dizziness | requires=fluids
malnutrition | is_a=condition | occurs_when=a diet lacks the energy or nutrients a body needs | causes=stunted growth | causes=weakened immunity

# --- practice and prevention ---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
surgery | is_a=medical treatment | means=treating by operating on the body | requires=anaesthesia | requires=sterile technique
anaesthesia | is_a=medical procedure | purpose=preventing pain during surgery | has_kind=general anaesthesia | has_kind=local anaesthesia
X ray | is_a=imaging technique | purpose=seeing bone and dense tissue | discoverer=Wilhelm Rontgen | requires=ionising radiation
MRI | means=magnetic resonance imaging | is_a=imaging technique | purpose=seeing soft tissue in detail | has_property=no ionising radiation
ultrasound | is_a=imaging technique | purpose=imaging soft tissue and a fetus | requires=sound waves | has_property=safe in pregnancy
blood test | is_a=diagnostic test | purpose=measuring what is in the blood
first aid | is_a=practice | purpose=giving immediate help before professional care arrives | involves=stopping bleeding | involves=keeping an airway open
CPR | means=cardiopulmonary resuscitation | is_a=emergency procedure | purpose=keeping blood and oxygen moving when the heart stops | involves=chest compressions
sanitation | is_a=public health measure | purpose=separating waste from drinking water | causes=a large fall in infectious disease
handwashing | is_a=hygiene practice | purpose=removing pathogens from the hands | causes=less transmission of infection
exercise | is_a=physical activity | causes=a stronger heart | causes=better mood | causes=better blood sugar control | requires=regularity to help
sleep | is_a=biological process | purpose=restoring the body and consolidating memory | requires=regular timing | causes=poor concentration when short
balanced diet | is_a=eating pattern | consists_of=carbohydrate | consists_of=protein | consists_of=fat | consists_of=vitamins | consists_of=minerals | consists_of=fibre | purpose=supplying what the body needs
smoking | is_a=health risk | causes=lung cancer | causes=heart disease | causes=chronic lung disease
